{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqf82fketm9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"AUTO mode loop autostart: permission_mode payload field plus ORCH_AUTO_LOOP env fallback","summary":"Implemented loop default-on in auto mode (task 0b5a907e/4). Detection path: classify.sh forwards the UserPromptSubmit payload field permission_mode to POST /classify, and the daemon treats bypassPermissions and acceptEdits as auto mode. Because the real payload could not be captured in this background-worker context (the orch write gate blocks instrumenting the installed hook, and no prior capture existed at /tmp/orch-uphook-capture.jsonl), I implemented BOTH paths so correctness does not depend on the unverified field: permission_mode from the payload AND an explicit env fallback ORCH_AUTO_LOOP=1 forwarded as auto_mode:true. When auto mode plus ready tasks plus no active session loop, the daemon starts the loop itself via lib/loop-autostart.js (config tokenBudget 80000 maxIterations 100 minPoll 30 maxPoll 300 batch 4 maxConcurrency 6) and emits \"[Orchestrator] Auto-started loop ID (auto mode)\" instead of the soft nudge. Idempotent on an active same-session loop. Opt-out is naturally respected: classify.sh exits before relaying for orch-off sessions. Starting a loop does NOT auto-merge (note:note-mq561rur preserved). FOLLOWUP: a maintainer with an interactive auto-mode session should confirm Claude Code actually emits permission_mode; if it does, the env fallback is redundant but harmless.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T13:01:33.902Z","vec":[-0.09849768877029419,0.04008650779724121,-0.06403357535600662,-0.04527714475989342,0.061689555644989014,-0.03380906954407692,0.0486433207988739,0.017459822818636894,-0.07766731828451157,0.0005118916160427034,0.004732985515147448,-0.024108057841658592,-0.022366568446159363,0.00360558251850307,-0.0061139194294810295,0.024657951667904854,0.08625401556491852,-0.03391590341925621,-0.036700598895549774,-0.06596832722425461,0